My cloth bags are now full.
They are very heavy.
I check my watch.
The time is ten o'clock.
I am very happy.
I walk out of the crowd in the market.
There are a few autos parked there.
I go near an auto.
"Can you come near my house?" I ask the driver.
"I will come," he says.
"How much is it to get there?" I ask.
"One hundred and fifty rupees," he replies.
I agree to that.
He helps to put my bags in the auto.
I get into the auto.
The auto goes forward.
I look outside.
Today's shopping went very well.
